A||||9||87fiero_gt||V6 firing order
Z||000000||87fiero_gt||06-28-99||05:22 PM||||Lost my mark when changing the dist. I need to verify the firing order. right side 1,3,5 from front to back. Left side 2,4,6 from front to back and 1,2,3,4,5,6 is that right.<br>Also what is the best way to make sure I posistion the dist correctly. Does the thing turn clockwise or counter?<br>
Z||000001||Stroker||06-28-99||06:45 PM||||  87fiero_gt, <br>           The way I tell everybody which cylider bank is which is this: open the rear deck-lid then stand on the passenger side and look at the front of the engine (the side where the belt(s) are, of course).<br>  Now,the left-hand(or trunk) side is the 1,3,5 cylinder bank. The right(or firewall) side is the 2,4,6 cyl. bank.<br>  The distributor rotates to your RIGHT(or counter-clockwise).<br>  Re-index your distributor by taking out the #1 sparkplug, rotating your crank to the 0 degree hash mark on the timing cover, and installing the dist. with the module connectors facing toward the EGR valve or just slightly to the right of it as you look at it from the drivers side rear. <br>  To make sure you are on the COMPRESSION STROKE, have a friend place his finger over the #1 hole as you bring it around to the 0 mark, THEN install the distributor.<br>           Let us know!!!
Z||000002||batboy||06-28-99||06:46 PM||||The firing order is correct: 1-2-3-4-5-6<br>The front bank of cylinders (facing towards the front of the car) is 2-4-6 with #6 closest to the distributor. The rear bank (closest to the tail of the car) is 1-3-5 with #5 being closest to the distributor. Rotation of the distributor is clockwise as you are looking down from above.
Z||000003||batboy||06-28-99||06:51 PM||||Stroker, I think you have an echo (haha). Yes I agree, find #1 top dead center and reset the distributor.
Z||000004||Stroker||06-28-99||06:53 PM||||I meant CLOCKWISE, the distributor rotates clokwise.(wish I could've corrected that)<br>              Sorry.
Z||000005||87fiero_gt||06-28-99||06:54 PM||||Stroker, to me if it turns to the right, that is clockwise. Are we talking the same thing here? I've got two different answers.
Z||000006||Stroker||06-28-99||07:11 PM||||87fiero_gt,<br>          We are all on the same sheet of music. You are correct, clockwise IS to the right. <br>  I just mistyped in my first reply.
Z||000007||87fiero_gt||06-28-99||07:24 PM||||Sorry stroker, I posted before I saw your reply. My old dist had an arrow on the flange but I don't seem to be able to locate anything to match it up with. Anyway I bought this car for my son so I'm not real familiar with fieros or anything else apparently. What does the EGR valve look like. Help me!! And where is the tach filter?<br>Thanks for your help.
Z||000008||Stroker||06-28-99||07:44 PM||||87fiero_gt, The EGR valve is located on the crossover pipe of the exhaust system. The pipe runs over the transaxle bellhousing and the EGR valve is the round device which is about 3.5 inches in diameter and sits almost in the middle of this pipe.<br>     As for the tach filter, OGRE or GREENDANO help this man please.<br>
Z||000009||GREENDANO||06-28-99||09:01 PM||||Thanks Stroker, I'll take that as a complement!  <br>  The tach filter is the little round, silver can about 1/2" in diameter and about 1 1/4" long.  It connects to the tach lead coming out of the ignition module and "cleans up" the output of the ignition module so the tach in the instrument panel can get a clean input.  It's bolted to the coil bracket area.  I just got a filter out of a Lumina van and will be replacing mine maybe this weekend because my tach jumps sometimes durring acceleration.  I'll keep everyone up to date.<br>  Dan-O<br>  
